%I A401522 #10 Nov 10 2026 15:36:00
%S A401522 1,4,54,1916,155840,28340772,11732200032,11225844545624,
%T A401522 24846527358647712,125964155316889586720,1442010308194870564762832,
%U A401522 36740043172185945799285248084,2056981211691929101557828913894896,250434303384776105160318592791266320124
%N A401522 Number of digraphs on n labeled nodes that are reducible for every election of source-SCC headers: each choice of one node per source SCC makes the virtual-rooted flow graph reducible.
%C A401522 An election chooses one node in each source strongly connected component (one receiving no edge from outside). Join a new root to the chosen nodes to obtain a flow graph.
%C A401522 Differs from the some-election count first at n = 3, precisely by the strong digraphs reducible from some but not every node (smallest: edges 12, 13, 23, 32, 21, reducible from nodes 2 and 3 but not node 1).
%C A401522 A digraph qualifies iff every non-source SCC is a single-entry region (weight m*W(m), W = A397470) and every source SCC is reducible from every node (weight V(m)=A400123(m)).
%C A401522 Each qualifying digraph is counted once, not once for each election. All digraphs here have no self-loops. In the formula, DAG(k) is the set of acyclic digraphs on nodes 1,...,k, src(H) denotes its sources, W(m)=A397470(m), and V(m)=A400123(m).
%D A401522 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A401522 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A401522 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A401522 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A401522 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401522/b401522.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..48</a>
%H A401522 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A401522 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A401522 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Python program (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%F A401522 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} (1/k!) * Sum_{m_1+...+m_k=n; m_i>=1} multinomial(n;m_1,...,m_k) * Sum_{H in DAG(k)} Product_{i in src(H)} V(m_i) * Product_{i not in src(H)} m_i*W(m_i) * Product_{(i,j) in E(H)} (2^m_i-1).
%o A401522 (Python)
%o A401522 # Save the three linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A401522 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A401522 from valid_header_elections import valid_header_sequence
%o A401522 valid_header_sequence("labeled_reducible_digraphs_every", 20)
